# Project documentation
CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
STANDARDS_STATUS.md
TRADING_PARTNER_VERIFICATION.md
*_VERIFICATION.md

# Internal analysis/investigation briefs stay local, not in the remote repo.
*_ANALYSIS.md
OAUTH_DISCONNECT_ANALYSIS.md

# Documentation and development records are NOT part of this public repository: docs/
# is a local-only folder on the maintainer's machine. Product specifications live in
# specs/, test fixtures in tests/fixtures/, generated reference pages in reference/.
# Anchored, so it never reaches a nested docs/ directory elsewhere in the tree.
/docs/

# Test files (local only, except anywhere under tests/)
test_*.py
!tests/**/test_*.py
# Root-level scratch analysis scripts only. MUST stay anchored (leading /): an
# unanchored analyze_*.py matched the tracked package module
# src/boomi_mcp/categories/components/analyze_component.py at any depth, which
# gcloud (via .gitignore-derived upload exclusions) then dropped from local
# `gcloud builds submit` contexts, silently disabling 4 tool categories.
/analyze_*.py

# Agents (local only)
agents/

# Tasks (local only)
tasks/

# Lock files (local only)
.~lock.*

# Vendored FastMCP (replaced by upstream v3.1.1 via pip)
fastmcp/

# Incident investigation bundles
incident-*/

# Boomi companion local workspace (autogenerated, stays local)
/boomi_companion/

# Zero-license no-op QA fixture provisioner + its account-specific state (local)
scripts/provision_qa_noop_fixture.py
scripts/.qa_noop_fixture_pins.json*

# Live-account inventory dumps written by QA capture runs. Ignored at EVERY depth, then
# re-included under the checksummed Boomi fixture tree only (a capture's SHA256SUMS lists
# them, and .gcloudignore inherits these rules, so a force-add alone would still drop them
# from the build-context upload).
*_liveness.json
!tests/fixtures/boomi/**/*_liveness.json
